; WildGrass — Wild grass terrain visual. Emits NOTHING; deliberately tag-inert, and that
; inertness is load-bearing (terrain.md). This is what untouched revealed land looks like, and
; spec.md Open Question #29 is still open on it: it must read as "something to claim" without
; reading as broken.
;
; STILL EXACTLY ONE VARIANT, AND THAT IS A DELIBERATE HOLD, NOT AN OMISSION. Meadow and Scrub
; each went to 3 variants in this pass; Wild grass did not, because its `model_scenes` count is
; not a look decision here — it is wired into behaviour. `wild_grass` is one of only two style
; PICKER categories, so a second variant would make `WorldRoot._supports_mixed()` true, put a
; `mixed` row at the head of its catalog, and move its unchosen default off "wild_grass" onto
; "mixed" for every existing save (the same consequence D-54 accepted for Forest, but never
; ruled on for this terrain). Four test assertions pin the current state deliberately —
; test_hud_hotbar.gd's `style_ids_for_category("wild_grass").size() == 1`, two stale-id
; fallbacks in test_style_defaults.gd and one in test_save_round_trip.gd.
;
; RULED 2026-09-08 -> D-56: "wild grass should only have a single type". This is now a STANDING
; CONSTRAINT, not an unfinished look pass. Do not add a second variant here without a fresh
; human ruling, and do not re-point those four assertions to make one fit — they are the guard
; on that decision, not stale scaffolding. Improving this terrain's LOOK is still fair game
; (Open Question #29 is untouched and open); doing it by adding a variant is not.
;
; REBUILT THROUGH THE SHARED GENERATOR (2026-09-08) with its own values carried over unchanged:
; slab Color(0.55, 0.52, 0.3) olive-khaki, 3 bare-dirt patches Color(0.42, 0.34, 0.2), 32x
; Grass_Common_Short at the shorter 0.065 baseline, seed 20260816 — all of it the state the
; human's 2026-08-16 density/height feedback settled.
;
; CLUSTERED, NOT EVENLY SCATTERED, and this is the one place the shared generator's scatter is
; overridden: the 32 blades are distributed across 4 uneven clump centres with real bare ground
; between them. An even scatter would read as a mown lawn, which is precisely the opposite of
; "untouched" — the distinction from true Grass is the whole job of this tile.
;
; BUILT BY A ONE-OFF HEADLESS SCRIPT, NOT HAND-AUTHORED, AND NOT EDITABLE BY HAND — same
; generator, buffer layout and headless caveat as the four Grass variants; see
; GrassCommonShort.tscn's header for the full explanation. Re-run the generator to change
; anything below; do not hand-edit the MultiMesh buffer.
;
; INHERITS THE GRASS CALIBRATION BASELINE (human sign-off 2026-09-08): slab BoxMesh
; 1.0 x 0.2 x 1.0 at y=-0.1 (the 1.0 width is the cross-tile seam-gap fix, do not narrow it),
; blotchy floor patches at y=0.001, fixed-seed deterministic scatter within +/-0.42 tile-units
; of centre, +/-18% scale jitter and free Y-rotation, everything ground-level nested under one
; node named "Slab" (the OcclusionFader exemption convention). The human ruled on these values
; against Grass first precisely so they would not be re-proposed per terrain.
;
; HIGH-COUNT BLADES ARE A MULTIMESH; LOW-COUNT PROPS ARE INSTANCED glTF SCENES. Props here
; number 1-3 per tile, so a MultiMesh would buy nothing, and two of the flower meshes carry
; TWO surfaces with different textures, which a single embedded MultiMesh mesh cannot express
; cleanly. Referencing the raw piece directly is also what Meadow.tscn and Scrub.tscn already
; did before this pass.
;
; Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — License.txt
; re-checked per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate. See
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; GRASS COLOUR: DELIBERATELY DRIER BAND (2026-09-08 human ruling — "keep them drier").
; See GrassCommonShort.tscn's header for the full palette-band explanation. This terrain is
; deliberately NOT moved to band 2's true green: dryness is part of what distinguishes it from
; true Grass, and that distinction carries gameplay meaning (Scrub is `browse` rough grazing;
; Wild grass is tag-inert unclaimed land). It samples band 4, rgb(103,163,0) yellow-green —
; still a real change where the mesh shipped on band 1's gold, but visibly drier than Grass.
